        skos:definition        "A shipwreck refers to the physical remains of a ship that has either been sunk or beached. Whatever the cause, a sunken ship or a wrecked ship is a physical remnant of the event: this explains why the two concepts are often overlapping in English."@en , "Un naufragio se refiere a los restos físicos de un barco que ha sido hundido o varado."@es;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/ICANCOERO/current/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/MIDA/current/>;
